ASSESSMENT: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) Controls
TARGET INSTANCE: Isolated Gruyere Sandbox; instance identifier redacted
DATE: 2026-10-25

TEST PROCEDURE:
1. Navigated to the authenticated user's snippet-management interface.
2. Inspected the anchor href associated with the snippet-removal action.

OBSERVED BEHAVIOR:
- The removal control targeted the deletesnippet endpoint with an index parameter.
- Request method: GET
- No anti-CSRF token was visible in the inspected link.

LIMITATION:
No cross-origin request was sent and no deletion was triggered as part of this review. Cross-origin behavior was not tested.

CONCLUSION:
The inspected control has a CSRF-relevant design weakness because a state-changing action appears to use GET and the link contains no visible anti-CSRF token. This observation alone does not confirm a successful CSRF exploit.
